      "comment": "CREEPING TIGER (5) has some solid form under his belt and proved too strong last time to win by 8 lengths at Goulburn in a handy 19.83 beating Sutton Blend. Has hit winning form and can measure up again. SCOTT WEDNESDAY (1) carved over from wide out and boxed on strongly to finish 1.75 lengths away in second (18.74) behind Fantastic Tariq at Richmond. Goes well out of this box with a win and three minor placings. Expected to feature again. HUMBLE SMILES (2) has been beaten for early speed lately, last time finishing fourth (19.53) in a Grade 5 at this track. One of the better hopes. JET'S DIGGER (8) can feature with the right run.",
